            ]
          },
          "notes": []
        },
        {
          "role": "second",
          "ref": "Colossians 3:1-4",
          "refKey": "Col.3.1-Col.3.4",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "call-and-discipleship",
              "hope-and-promise",
              "resurrection-and-life"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "assurance",
              "exhortation"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 3,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "If ye are risen, seek the things above — As Christ being risen, immediately went to heaven."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 3,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "For ye are dead — To the things on earth. And your real, spiritual life is hid from the world, and laid up in God, with Christ - Who hath merited, promised, prepared it for us, and gives us the earnest and foretaste of it in our hearts."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 3,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "When Christ — The abruptness of the sentence surrounds us with sudden light. Our life - The fountain of holiness and glory. Shall appear - In the clouds of heaven."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "gospel",
          "ref": "John 20:1-18",
          "refKey": "John.20.1-John.20.18",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faith-and-trust",
              "mission-and-witness",
              "resurrection-and-life"
            ],
            "image": [
              "garden",
              "tomb-and-grave"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "joy",
              "wonder-and-awe"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "Matt. xxviii, 1; Mark xvi, 1; Luke xxiv, 1."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "Peter went out — Of the city."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "Peter seeth the linen clothes lie — and the napkin folded up - The angels who ministered to him when he rose, undoubtedly folded up the napkin and linen clothes."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "He saw — That the body was not there, and believed - That they had taken it away as Mary said."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "For as yet — They had no thought of his rising again."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "They went home — Not seeing what they could do farther."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "But Mary stood — With more constancy. Mark xvi, 9."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 16,
              "v_end": 16,
              "text": "Jesus saith to her, Mary — With his usual voice and accent."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 20,
              "v_start": 17,
              "v_end": 17,
              "text": "Touch me not — Or rather, Do not cling to me (for she held him by the feet,) Matt. xxviii, 9. Detain me not now. You will have other opportunities of conversing with me. For I am not ascended to my Father - I have not yet left the world. But go immediately to my brethren -- thus does he intimate in the strongest manner the forgiveness of their fault, even without ever mentioning it. These exquisite touches, which everywhere abound in the evangelical writings, show how perfectly Christ knew our frame. I ascend - He anticipates it in his thoughts, and so speaks of it as a thing already present. To my Father and your Father, to my God and your God - This uncommon expression shows that the only- begotten Son has all kind of fellowship with God. And a fellowship with God the Father, some way resembling his own, he bestows upon his brethren. Yet he does not say, Our God: for no creature can be raised to an equality with him: but my God and your God: intimating that the Father is his in a singular and incommunicable manner; and ours through him, in such a kind as a creature is capable of."
            }
          ]
        }
